@startuml http_session_update
' Source baseline: pi-mono-java 09b32d8ea4a4b43b34be302d8b2745bdc417c9a2.
' Source: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/persistence/MyBatisRuntimeSessionRepository.java :: rejectConfigurationUpdate, appendConfigurationEntries.
' Source: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/session/RuntimeSessionResponseAssembler.java :: getView.
' Observed behavior: existing configuration writes use row locks and durable events.
' Design reason: resolve a combined target before a single version-checked transaction.
' Java divergence: unified POST and atomic four-property update are target-only.
title Unified Session POST - Target Transaction
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam maxMessageSize 230
autonumber
actor Caller
participant "RuntimeSessionController" as API
participant "Configuration application\nand shared validation" as App
participant "Model Manager" as Models
participant "Session Repository" as Repo
database GaussDB as DB
participant "Response assembler\nand ETag factory" as Response
Caller -> API : POST /sessions/{sessionId}\nIf-Match + submitted fields
API -> API : Strict VO binding\nReject null, unknown, duplicate or readonly keys
API -> App : updateSession(sessionId, ifMatch, requestVO)
App -> Repo : read current Session
Repo --> App : current values and resource version
App -> App : Precheck version and field-based admission\nNormalize name; derive final model first
opt modelId submitted or thinking=true
  App -> Models : Resolve required model and capabilities
  Models --> App : Validated model snapshot, or failure
end
App -> App : Validate final thinking and plan availability\nBuild immutable candidate with expectedVersion
App -> Repo : updateConfiguration(candidate)
group One transaction
  Repo -> DB : SELECT Session FOR UPDATE
  DB --> Repo : authoritative current Session
  Repo -> Repo : Recheck existence, version and field-based idle
  alt validation fails or version/state changed
    Repo --> App : Reject entire update; no fields/events committed
  else all final values equal
    Repo --> App : UNCHANGED; original Session and version
  else real changes
    Repo -> DB : Update all changed properties\nAdvance updated_at/resource_version once
    Repo -> DB : Append changed model, thinking, mode events in order\nNo name event
    DB --> Repo : Commit all, or roll back all
    Repo --> App : UPDATED; committed Session DTO
  end
end
alt accepted
  App -> Response : getView(committed DTO)
  Response --> App : Session response VO + same-snapshot ETag
  App --> API : RuntimeSessionView
  API --> Caller : 200 ResultBean<Session>\nETag + no-store
else rejected
  API --> Caller : HTTP error + resCode/resMsg\nNo partial-success fields
end
note over Caller,DB
  Name-only updates may run during execution.
  An execution field requires idle, even when unchanged.
  This POST never starts inference or approves a plan.
  On an uncertain response, GET before deciding to retry.
end note
@enduml
